<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτλαντικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of Atlas,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρμονες Ἀ.</span> the pillars of
			Hercules, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1053
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Ἀ. πέλαγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					24e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				946a29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἀ. θάλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					392b22
				</span></i>
			:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτλάντειος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Critias
				18.5
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>:— fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτλαντίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, as
			Patron., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				938
			</span></i>; title of work by Hellanicus (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτλαντιάς</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὁμηρίδαι</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; θάλασσα ἡ Ἀ. καλουμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.202
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἀ. νῆσος,</span> a fabulous
			island in the far West, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				25a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				2.3.6
			</span></i>.</div>
